 # Physics and Optical Modeling
 
-Also called: Volumetric Attenuation, Underwater 3DGS, Continuous Attenuation
 
 ## Overview
-Physics and Optical Modeling extends the standard 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) representation to handle non-vacuum media and physically consistent surface extraction by modifying the rendering equation or the underlying density field [G]. It solves the problem of light transport in scattering media (e.g., underwater fog) and the geometric inconsistency of discrete alpha-blending for surface reconstruction [G]. Unlike [Color and Appearance Modeling](14740-color-and-appearance-modeling.md), which focuses on view-dependent shading and material properties in clear space, this family explicitly models volumetric attenuation and backscatter or reformulates the Gaussian primitive as a continuous attenuation field [G].
